  "gitCommitMessage": "feat(updates): wire EAS Update with fingerprint runtime policy\n\nInstalls expo-updates and configures OTA delivery so JS-only changes\n(UI, logic, AI prompts, sheets, screens) can ship via\n  npx eas update --channel preview --message \"...\"\nwithout a full APK rebuild. Only native changes (new native deps,\nplugin config edits, etc.) require a fresh EAS build.\n\napp.json:\n- Adds \"expo-updates\" to plugins\n- expo.updates: url + checkAutomatically: ON_LOAD (poll on cold start)\n  + fallbackToCacheTimeout: 0 (don't block boot waiting for the network)\n- expo.runtimeVersion: { policy: \"fingerprint\" } — EAS auto-computes a\n  hash of the native side per build; OTAs only land on builds with\n  matching fingerprint, so native dep changes naturally gate updates\n  to a fresh build without manual version bumps.\n\neas.json:\n- Each build profile (development/preview/production) gets a matching\n  channel: \"<name>\" so the published APK polls the right update feed.\n\nCaveats:\n- Existing preview APKs (#10, #11) were built before this config and\n  will NOT receive OTA updates. The next preview build creates the\n  first APK that polls \"preview\" channel.\n- The native fingerprint changes on this commit (added expo-updates\n  module), so build #12 will be a fresh native compile. Subsequent\n  JS-only commits land via `eas update`.\n\nWorkflow going forward:\n  Native change (deps, plugins, android/ios edits)\n    → npx eas build --profile preview --platform android\n  Pure JS/TS/asset change\n    → npx eas update --channel preview --message \"what changed\"\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
